  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `DataFiles::from_process` (`crates/post/src/data_dir.rs`) resolves the executable path with the new `real_exe` before the assets lookup. If the path is a symbolic link, `real_exe` gives the real file (`std::fs::canonicalize`). The lookup then starts in the install folder, not in the folder of the link. The posts and the machines use this lookup.\n- `real_exe` changes only a link. A plain path keeps its form, so a Windows path in a message gets no `\\\\?\\` prefix. A link that does not resolve keeps the link path, and the refusal names the folder of the link, as before.\n- The refusal of a copy of the executable now ends with `COPY_HINT`: \"Start the program from its install folder, or through a symbolic link to the installed executable: a copy of the executable has no assets beside it.\" No setting or environment variable points at an assets folder, so the hint names none.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3028-symlink-exe-posts.md`.\n\n## Readings (Linux, Manjaro, release build of `camcraft-cli`)\n\nInstall-style folder: `install/camcraft-cli` and `install/assets/{posts,machines}`, outside a cargo build tree. Command: `camcraft-cli process examples/catalog/2d/first-part/first-part.camproj -o out.nc`.\n\n| Started as | Before this change | With this change |\n|---|---|---|\n| `install/camcraft-cli` | rc 0, 369 lines | rc 0, 369 lines |\n| `bin/camcraft-cli`, a symbolic link to the installed file | rc 0, 369 lines | rc 0, 369 lines, the same bytes as the install run |\n| `copy/camcraft-cli`, a copy | rc 1, \"no posts folder found ...\" | rc 1, the same refusal, then the `COPY_HINT` text |\n\nOn Linux, `current_exe` reads `/proc/self/exe`, which is already the real file. Thus the symlink case worked on Linux before this change. The fix is for macOS and Windows, where `current_exe` gives the link path.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `data_dir::tests::a_symlinked_exe_finds_the_assets_beside_the_real_file` (Unix only: a symbolic link on Windows needs a privilege). It also checks a chain of two links, a dangling link, and the old result for the link path.\n- `data_dir::tests::a_copied_exe_is_refused_with_the_fix`.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 3 steps, 0 failed (`post build`, `post suites: lib`, `post suites: folder_scan`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: the diff reaches the 200 app heavy steps through the crate dependency. Result on head 009623a59: 200 steps, 1 failed, 48.3 min.\n  - The three known-fail steps (#1950, #2845, #2849) are red as expected.\n  - Red: `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm`, test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`. It gives (3158, 3130, 1141). The Linux x86_64 pin is (4726, 4698, 549).\n  - The same test on unchanged `upstream/main` at 3c761b5bb fails with the same counts. This PR does not cause it: the test plans a toolpath and reads no posts or machines folder. Issue #3050 (P2) tracks this stale pin. Its body names the same counts on Windows and a stale Linux pin after PR #2904.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- macOS and Windows. I have no machine for them. The macOS cause is the one in the issue. `std::env::current_exe` documents that it can give the path of a symbolic link. A Windows reading is still necessary for the third \"Done means\" item.\n- `crates/ui/src/theme_dir.rs` finds `assets/themes` with `current_exe` too, and has the same link behaviour. The desktop app is not usually started through a link, so this PR does not change it. A follow-up issue can track it if the maintainer wants that.\n\nChangelog: A `camcraft-cli` started through a symbolic link (the usual macOS PATH set-up) finds the shipped posts and machines beside the real executable. A copy of the executable is still refused, and the message now says how to start it.\n\nFork synced at v0.24.0; branch made from `upstream/main` at 3c761b5bb.\n\nFixes #3028\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
